        "part": null
      },
      "marker": null,
      "ordered": null,
      "rows": null,
      "section_path": [
        "Sick Leave Reporting Guide",
        "Record the period"
      ],
      "text": "The paid sick allowances are 10 days for Contract A, 5 for B, and 12 for C per calendar year. Nonworking roster days do not consume the balance. Paid sick days do not carry over. A report does not guarantee payment; HR checks eligibility and the available balance under Sick Pay & Absence Policy. Do not request annual leave merely because a sick balance is exhausted.",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "heading_level": 2,
      "is_semantic": true,
      "list_level": null,
      "location": {
        "bbox": [
          63.599998474121094,
          381.3899841308594,
          221.08197021484375,
          399.2909851074219
        ],
        "element": null,
        "line": null,
        "page": 1,
        "part": null
      },
      "marker": null,
      "ordered": null,
      "rows": null,
      "section_path": [
        "Sick Leave Reporting Guide",
        "Evidence and notification"
      ],
      "text": "Evidence and notification",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "heading_level": null,
      "is_semantic": true,
      "list_level": null,
      "location": {
        "bbox": [
          63.599998474121094,
          404.5124816894531,
          531.0707397460938,
          476.9394836425781
        ],
        "element": null,
        "line": null,
        "page": 1,
        "part": null
      },
      "marker": null,
      "ordered": null,
      "rows": null,
      "section_path": [
        "Sick Leave Reporting Guide",
        "Evidence and notification"
      ],
      "text": "Self-certification covers up to three consecutive scheduled workdays in one sickness episode. Evidence is required from the fourth scheduled workday and should be uploaded within two business days of that threshold. Consecutive episodes separated only by nonworking days count as one episode. Managers receive the absence dates and coverage impact, while medical attachments remain restricted to HR absence administrators.",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "heading_level": 2,
      "is_semantic": true,
      "list_level": null,
      "location": {
        "bbox": [
